+# Automation provider-limit outcomes
+
+Status: implementation applied; completion gate blocked by unrelated full-suite failures. Scope: provider notices returned as successful assistant output.
+
+- [x] Reproduce provider-limit completions being recorded as successful runs (34 regression failures before the fix).
+- [x] Recognise usage/spend notices without matching ordinary output discussing limits.
+- [x] Fail tracked automation runs before success bookkeeping on every completion path.
+- [ ] Verify focused regressions, project gates, and an independent fresh-agent review.
+
+Implementation: tighten the shared notice detector and check it at the runner's common success boundary. Preserve output summaries and existing failure/retry bookkeeping. Do not alter thread-delivery or loop lifecycle semantics.
+
+As-built: the runner uses provider `accumulatedContent` when present, including empty terminal flushes, so a raw streaming suffix cannot determine the run outcome. The common success boundary classifies the complete message before success stamps, persistence, outcome streaks and retries. The shared detector requires notice-shaped statements, supports usage/quota/spend/credit refusals, and ignores ordinary reset/quota/request prose.
+
+Verification:
+
+- 154 focused tests passed, including streaming complete/idle, empty flush, reconciliation and retry coverage. Streaming regressions reproduced 39 failures before the accumulation fix.
+- Both TypeScript checks, lint, LOC ratchet, main build and renderer build passed on the final patch.
+- Final full suite: 24,520 tests, 14 failures in 6 unrelated files; command exited 1. Failures: `worker-node-exec-policy.spec.ts` (1), `worker-rpc-dispatcher.node-ops.spec.ts` (3), `check-ts-max-loc.spec.ts` (5), `dependency-compatibility.spec.ts` (1), `sea-build-repeatability.spec.ts` (2), `capability-probe.spec.ts` (2). Observed causes include restricted process operations, missing `tsx/dist/cli.cjs`, installed dependency-tree mismatches, and capability readiness assertions.
+- A fresh completion review found the streaming issue; it was fixed and reviewed by another fresh agent. The second verifier independently passed 154 focused tests, 155 adjacent tests, both typechecks and lint, and found no actionable patch issues. Its strict overall verdict remains FAIL because full-suite Gate 0 is not green.
+
+Evidence is in ignored `_scratch/provider-limit-final-*.log` and `_scratch/independent-provider-gate-*.log` files. The plan remains active and untracked because full verification has not passed; no live-test deferral or completion claim applies.
